<p class="mt-align-center"><span class="&lt;p"><img alt="the=" data-height="74" data-width="358" style="width: 302px; height: 62px;" width="302px" height="62px" class="internal" loading="lazy" src="https://chem.libretexts.org/@api/deki/files/461050/cf18ebd7e8cb596c6f9b36dc231279f6f0c1e516?revision=1&amp;size=bestfit&amp;width=302&amp;height=62" /> </span></p>

<p class="lt-chem-459808"><span class="&lt;p">An illustration shows the structure of diketo dialdehyde. It shows two carbonyl groups single bonded to each other. Each carbonyl group is bonded to a chain of three methylene groups and then to an aldehyde group.</span></p>

<ul>
    <li><span class="&lt;p">(a) </span>Propose two possible structures for <b>A</b>.</li>
